                        ],
                        "form": "претенцио́зностях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b7377292-7ff3-3172-a171-615c0caf8e7d",
                        "entry_id": "5db8a2b2-4e14-3d54-904a-3260d25bfd3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн., неодобр. свойство по значению прилагательного претенциозный; неоправданная усложнённость, вычурность, манерность, основанная на претензиях, желании произвести впечатление"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "06f9045f-029c-4b42-9a91-7ace81d79af6",
                                "sense_id": "b7377292-7ff3-3172-a171-615c0caf8e7d",
                                "text": "Насколько я презираю бездарную претенциозность, настолько же преклоняюсь искренне перед талантом, серьезным и искренним."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d68c6bb-afec-486b-b7a4-41f6397e7f17",
                                "sense_id": "b7377292-7ff3-3172-a171-615c0caf8e7d",
                                "text": "Несмотря на дикость и претенциозность интерьера, в нем присутствовала своеобразная мрачная эстетика, завораживающая зрителя."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e32294b9-5515-391c-b546-a1ca1f5a1f85",
                        "entry_id": "5db8a2b2-4e14-3d54-904a-3260d25bfd3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. требовательность, неуместно высокая самооценка"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "05337efc-0909-428a-af7c-9cd544123fb7",
                        "source_entry_id": "5db8a2b2-4e14-3d54-904a-3260d25bfd3e",
                        "target_lang_word": "pretentiousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pretentiousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "460f4571-21d6-3c5a-8edc-6fde37595ba4",
                                        "entry_id": "554481e6-6ed2-3002-9df1-a305e625f734",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being pretentious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbf8f209-047e-4d84-9737-6f765068849d",
                                                "sense_id": "460f4571-21d6-3c5a-8edc-6fde37595ba4",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: affectation, affectedness, false pretense, pretending"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f20a907c-e3f4-4303-9f6e-071efd9e446e",
                                                "sense_id": "460f4571-21d6-3c5a-8edc-6fde37595ba4",
                                                "text": "Possibly her sheer pretentiousness, or that she knew everything about everything, or maybe because she treated her reporters like underoxygenated platypies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ac7b47fd-fa2c-4a39-9bc2-67ff0772d0d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "5db8a2b2-4e14-3d54-904a-3260d25bfd3e",
                        "target_lang_word": "affectation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "affectation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69ea6a0d-447c-39c8-8b17-8b6728dd1378",
                                        "entry_id": "b7931b8d-4e43-3934-96a0-da2e1a2131e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An attempt to assume or exhibit what is not natural or real; false display; artificial show."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c4f4156-3393-474b-a90d-78107f773696",
                                                "sense_id": "69ea6a0d-447c-39c8-8b17-8b6728dd1378",
                                                "text": "This poem is strongly tinctured with those pedantic affectations concerning the passion of love ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78902a0f-bae1-44d7-95de-210fb4790ba0",
                                                "sense_id": "69ea6a0d-447c-39c8-8b17-8b6728dd1378",
                                                "text": "[T]hey were not the spoiled children of affectation and refinement, but a bold, vigorous, independent race of thinkers, with prodigious strength and energy, with none but natural grace, and heartfelt unobtrusive delicacy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9eb08ea4-47be-3e1e-8113-a37f50d0f483",
                                        "entry_id": "b7931b8d-4e43-3934-96a0-da2e1a2131e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unusual mannerism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5444e6f2-571e-37a8-82a8-89fa7f4b95eb",
                                        "entry_id": "b7931b8d-4e43-3934-96a0-da2e1a2131e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ostentatious fondness for something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "with-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b67f58e-abb3-4115-a918-48c5319dc089",
                                                "sense_id": "5444e6f2-571e-37a8-82a8-89fa7f4b95eb",
                                                "text": "The grace diuineſt Mercvrie hath done me, / In this vouchſafde diſcouerie of himſelfe, / Binds my obſeruance in the vtmoſt terme / Of ſatisfaction, to his godly will: / Though I profeſſe (without the affectation / Of an enforc’d, and form’d auſteritie) / I could be willing to enioy no place / With ſo vnequall natures."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0250ba52-5340-467a-a55a-63e8d277cf39",
                                                "sense_id": "5444e6f2-571e-37a8-82a8-89fa7f4b95eb",
                                                "text": "Her upper part of decent diſcipline / Shew’d affecation of an ancient line: / And fathers, councils, church and churches head, / Were on her reverend Phylacteries read."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db3e4624-b956-4992-90ce-320db17d55bf",
                                                "sense_id": "5444e6f2-571e-37a8-82a8-89fa7f4b95eb",
                                                "text": "While for some, women’s lack of knowledge is a matter for censure, throughout the century both male and female writers emphasize that affectation of knowledge, for example when it is not properly assimilated (Du Bosc 1633: 78), and above all pedantry from women, are far more unacceptable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
